# Hand-build before the prebuilt

When a phase says to write the raw version first, do not jump to the library helper. The raw version goes in `labs/` or the app, and it must run before the library version.

- A tool-calling loop before `create_agent`.
- SQL retrieval and reciprocal rank fusion before a retriever class.
- A metric function before Ragas or DeepEval.
- Trimming and summarising before summarisation middleware.

If the raw version is not in the repo, help the user write it. Move to the library only after it runs and the user can explain what it does.

The user saying "use the library directly" overrides this. Note what they skipped.
